  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "If \\(2^{1998}-2^{1997}\\) \\({}-2^{1996}+2^{1995}\\) \\(=k\\cdot2^{1995},\\) what is the value of \\(k?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(3\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\)",
    "E": "\\(5\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Every term contains the factor \\(2^{1995}\\). For example, \\(2^{1998}=2^{1995}\\cdot2^3\\), so factoring out this common power changes the given equation to\n\\[\n2^{1995}(2^3-2^2-2+1)=k\\cdot2^{1995}.\n\\]\nSince \\(2^{1995}>0\\), we may divide both sides by it. Therefore\n\\[\nk=8-4-2+1=3.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(3\\), choice C.",
